# Java / Spring style

- Lombok: `@RequiredArgsConstructor`, `@Slf4j`; constructor injection only.
- Package-private `*ServiceImpl` / controllers when neighbors do the same.
- `@Transactional` on service impls (class-level like existing code).
- DTOs at API boundary — never return entities from controllers.
- Naming: `*DTO`, `*Entity`, `*Service`, `*ServiceImpl`, `*Repository`, `*Mapper`, `*Controller`.
- Constants: `@UtilityClass`; use `ProfileConstant` / `CacheConstant` / `AttributeConstant`.
- Comments only when intent is non-obvious. Spotless: `./mvnw spotless:apply`.

## Validation (request DTOs)

- Write DTOs: class + `@NotBlank(message = "...")` (see `ArticleSaveDTO`).
- Strong rules: `@NotEmpty` + `@Pattern(..., message = "...")` (see `RegistrationDTO`).
- Tiny bodies may be `record` + `@NotBlank` (see `RefreshTokenDTO`).
- Prefer explicit `message=`; do not rely on default messages.

## MapStruct

- Spring component model via compiler flag — no need for `componentModel = "spring"` on every mapper.
- Method names: `mapToDto` / `mapToEntity` / `mapTo*DTO`.
- Updates: `@MappingTarget`.
- Cross-feature: `@Mapper(uses = {UserMapper.class})`.
- On create/update from DTO → entity: ignore `id`, `ol`, audit fields, and sensitive fields not in the DTO (see `AuthMapper`).
- Nested flatten: `@Mapping(target = "username", source = "author.username")`.
